## Next: the actual response payload

Time to make the contract concrete. Here's a candidate shape for the MCP response — every decision we've made should appear in it. Reading this surfaces 4 remaining questions in one pass.

```json
{
  "tool": "get_current_work_context",
  "input_echo": {
    "since": "2026-05-06T05:00:00Z",
    "until": "2026-05-06T09:00:00Z",
    "artifact_hint": null
  },
  "clusters": [
    {
      "cluster_id": "ctx_a8f3d12c",
      "anchor_artifacts": [
        { "type": "file",  "provider": "local_fs", "id": "echo::src/normalize/types.ts", "label": "src/normalize/types.ts" },
        { "type": "conversation", "provider": "claude_code", "id": "claude_code:abc-123", "label": "session abc-123" }
      ],
      "atom_ids": ["evt_001", "evt_007", "evt_012", "evt_015"],
      "edges": [
        { "from": "evt_001", "to": "evt_007", "shared_artifacts": ["echo::src/normalize/types.ts"] },
        { "from": "evt_007", "to": "evt_012", "shared_artifacts": ["claude_code:abc-123"] },
        { "from": "evt_012", "to": "evt_015", "shared_artifacts": ["echo::src/normalize/types.ts", "claude_code:abc-123"] }
      ],
      "open_loop_hints": [
        { "atom_id": "evt_015", "hints": ["unresolved_assistant_q"] }
      ],
      "source_breakdown": { "claude_code": 2, "cursor": 1, "git": 1 },
      "time_range": { "from": "2026-05-06T06:42:11Z", "to": "2026-05-06T08:55:03Z" }
    }
  ],
  "atoms": {
    "evt_001": { /* full NormalizedContextEvent */ },
    "evt_007": { /* ... */ },
    "evt_012": { /* ... */ },
    "evt_015": { /* ... */ }
  },
  "truncation": { "atoms_returned": 4, "atoms_total_in_window": 4, "clusters_returned": 1, "clusters_total": 1 }
}
```

This sketch makes 4 decisions implicitly. The decisions:

**(D1) Multiple clusters.** Response is `clusters[]`, not `cluster`. If the time window contains disjoint work threads (you worked on the normalizer in the morning AND a different thing in the afternoon, no shared artifacts), both come back. Default ranking: most recent atom first. AI client decides which to attend to.

**(D2) `cluster_id` is deterministic-ephemeral.** Computed as `hash(sorted(atom_ids))` — same atoms = same id, but no storage. Lets follow-up questions ("tell me more about ctx_a8f3d12c") work within a session without a traces table. V2 can promote to persisted later.

**(D3) Open-loop hints pass through.** Atoms already carry `open_loop_hints` from item 016. V1.5 surfaces them in the cluster response without resolving them ("here's what looked unresolved; the AI client can decide what to do"). Resolution stays V2.

**(D4) Atoms returned inline (`atoms` map), not as pointers.** Same call, same response — no second MCP roundtrip. Cluster sections only carry `atom_ids`; the full atoms are looked up via the map. Keeps the JSON deduplicated when an atom appears in multiple clusters (rare but possible if we relax connected-component later).

Plus one explicit **truncation** field so the AI client knows whether it got everything or there's more.

**Three things to sanity-check before I move on:**

- **(D1)**: agree we return all disjoint clusters in the window? Or do you want "most recent cluster only, with a flag others exist"?
- **(D2)**: deterministic-ephemeral IDs OK, or do you want persisted traces from day one (V1.5 storage table)?
- Anything in the JSON above that looks wrong or missing?

