this is some of codex's suggestions. no need to blindly listen if you think the suggestions are invalid. • I agree with the direction CC landed on. This is the clean version:

  V1 goal = generalizable evidence atoms
  V1.5 goal = WorkTrace builder
  V2 goal = Resume Packet product experience

  That preserves the non-dev north star without exploding V1.

  Key Correction
  The important distinction is:

  Artifact = concrete observable handle
  Work Object = inferred cluster

  So an atom should not say:

  work_object = "ACME deal"

  It should say:

  artifacts = [
    salesforce:opportunity:123,
    gmail:thread:abc,
    person:email:jane@acme.com,
    claude_web:conversation:xyz
  ]

  Then the trace layer later infers:

  work_object = "ACME renewal deal"

  That is the right layering.

  V1 Atom Shape
  I’d keep the atom this small:

  interface NormalizedContextEvent {
    schema_version: 1;
    id: string; // CaptureEvent.id

    time: {
      occurred_at: string;
      observed_at?: string;
      duration_ms?: number;
      position?: {
        turn?: number;
        message?: number;
        tool_call?: number;
        version?: number;
      };
    };

    source: {
      app: string;       // codex, claude_code, cursor, gmail, salesforce
      surface?: string;  // chat, editor, email, crm_record, browser
      account?: string;
      raw_pointer: string;
    };

    actors: Array<{
      role: 'user' | 'assistant' | 'tool' | 'system' | string;
      name?: string;
      model?: string;
      provider?: string;
    }>;

    action: {
      kind: string;      // open vocab: message, edit, search, commit, salesforce:update
      verb?: string;
      input?: string;
      output?: string;
      status?: string;
    };

    artifacts: Array<{
      provider: string;  // local_fs, github, gmail, salesforce, slack, notion
      type: string;      // file, repo, thread, opportunity, doc, person
      id: string;        // provider-scoped stable id
      label?: string;
      locator?: string;  // path/url/title when useful for humans
    }>;

    context?: {
      visible?: string;
      selected?: string;
      ambient?: string;
    };

    state?: {
      kind: 'snapshot' | 'delta';
      value: unknown;
    };

    conversation?: {
      provider: string;
      session_id: string;
      turn_index?: number;
      parent_event_id?: string;
    };

    open_loop_hints?: string[];

    provenance: {
      source_event_id: string;
      raw_payload_hash?: string;
      extractor_version?: string;
      redacted_fields?: string[];
      parse_warnings?: string[];
    };
  }

  Important choices:

  - action.kind is an open string, not a closed enum.
  - artifact.type is an open string, not a closed enum.
  - artifact.provider + artifact.type + artifact.id is the identity base.
  - context is optional but first-class.
  - open_loop_hints are observable hints only, not resolved truth.
  - state is snapshot or delta. Do not force before/after.

  WorkTrace Later
  This is not V1 storage. It is inferred later:

  interface WorkTrace {
    trace_id: string;
    work_object: {
      label?: string;
      type?: string;
      confidence: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low';
    };
    atom_ids: string[];
    links: Array<{
      from_atom_id: string;
      to_atom_id: string;
      reason: string;
      confidence: 'high' | 'medium' | 'low';
    }>;
    open_loops: Array<{
      description: string;
      status: 'open' | 'resolved' | 'stale';
      evidence_atom_ids: string[];
    }>;
  }

  But for V1, I would define this only as the direction. Don’t build the full thing yet.

  One Pushback On CC
  They said V1 implements adapters for Cursor, Claude Code, Git. I’d include Codex too, since Codex is already now locally well-covered.

  So V1 local normalizer adapters should be:

  codex
  claude_code
  cursor
  git

  Everything else is future stress test, not implementation scope.

  Final Decision
  Choose Y.

  V1 should ship:

  - raw CaptureEvent unchanged
  - read-time normalizer
  - open artifact identity model
  - context field
  - open-loop hints
  - source/provenance discipline
  - adapters for current local sources

  V1 should not ship:

  - real work-object resolver
  - global ontology
  - CRM/legal/medical entity resolution
  - Resume Packet product layer
  - permanent normalized storage table

  That gives you a substrate that is not dev-specific, without pretending V1 can solve all professions immediately.

